{"seconds": 48.6, "exit": 0, "final": "After Kg3 Qxe1, the queen is attacked by the rook. But if White plays Rxe1, Black still won a whole rook. However, Kg1 allows Black to win the rook cleanly and continue attacking. Let me finalize the best line:\n\n**Best move: Qd2+** \n\nThe forcing main line is:\n1. Qd2+ Kg1 (if Kf1 Qxe1+ Kxe1 and Black is up material; if Kg3 Qxe1 and Black won the rook)\n2. Qxe1+ Kh2 (or Qf1)\n3. Qxh1 and Black has won both rooks for the queen (net +1 material) or continues attacking.\n\nThis is a **fork** motif - the queen on d2 gives check while attacking the undefended rook on e1, and after the king moves, the rook falls.\n\n**Coaching note:**\nWhen your queen can give check while attacking an undefended piece (here the rook), calculate if you can win it by force. Qd2+ forces the king to move, leaving e1 undefended, so Black captures the rook with check. Always look for checks that do double duty\u2014attacking the king and an undefended piece simultaneously is devastating for club players to defend.\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"Qd2+\", \"line\": [\"Qd2+\", \"Kg1\", \"Qxe1+\", \"Kh2\", \"Qxh1\", \"Kh3\"], \"motifs\": [\"fork\"]}\n```", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "r4r1k/pp4pp/2p5/3p1Pq1/3p4/1B1P1Q1P/PPP2KP1/4R2R b - - 3 19"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "r4r1k/pp4pp/2p5/3p1Pq1/3p4/1B1P1Q1P/PPP2KP1/4R2R b - - 3 19"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-legal_moves", "args": {"fen": "r4r1k/pp4pp/2p5/3p1Pq1/3p4/1B1P1Q1P/PPP2KP1/4R2R b - - 3 19"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r4r1k/pp4pp/2p5/3p1Pq1/3p4/1B1P1Q1P/PPP2KP1/4R2R b - - 3 19", "move": "Qe3+"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r4r1k/pp4pp/2p5/3p1Pq1/3p4/1B1P1Q1P/PPP2KP1/4R2R b - - 3 19", "move": "Qg3+"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r4r1k/pp4pp/2p5/3p1Pq1/3p4/1B1P1Q1P/PPP2KP1/4R2R b - - 3 19", "move": "Qh4+"}}, {"tool": "chess-ey